      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A quick sense-check helps.\n\nFor two positive speeds on equal distances, the average speed must lie between them.\nIt is usually closer to the slower speed than the simple arithmetic mean is.\n\nIf the two speeds are equal, the average is that same speed.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
